[1m[38;5;231mHow should the settings module be loaded by the page?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mScript tag global (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mAdd settings.js loaded before app.js, exposing window.APP_CONFIG. No tooling, index.html still opens from disk.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m ES modules
     [38;5;246mSwitch app.js to type="module" with import/export. Cleaner, but the page then needs a local server instead of [39m
     [38;5;246mfile://.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m CommonJS under src/
     [38;5;246mMatch src/utils.js style. Only works if a bundler or Node consumer is coming; the browser page can't require() it [39m
     [38;5;246mtoday.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Build-step env injection
     [38;5;246mAdd a bundler/dotenv toolchain that substitutes per-environment values at build time. Heaviest; adds the repo's [39m
     [38;5;246mfirst dependency.[39m
